.TITLE "mkdir"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Creates new directories. It allows you to build the __filesystem structure__ by generating one or more folders at specified paths.

.DIV "TLDR"
**mkdir folder_name**
Creates a single new directory in the current path.
> __folder_name__ name of the new directory

**mkdir -p path/to/directory**
Creates parent directories as needed to build a full path.
> __-p__ parents flag | __path/to/directory__ the full path structure

**mkdir -v folder_name**
Displays a message for each directory created.
> __-v__ verbose flag

**mkdir -m 755 folder_name**
Sets the file permissions (mode) for the new directory at the time of creation.
> __-m__ mode flag | __755__ octal permissions | __folder_name__ the new directory

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __-p__ flag is essential for automation and scripts, as it prevents errors if the directory already exists and ensures all necessary parent folders are created in one command.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:rm** **mac:ls**

